LogHawk Windows PySpark Setup Guide\par
\par
1. Why this is needed\par
PySpark on Windows needs a compatible JDK and a Hadoop WinUtils install.\par
If the Java version is not compatible with the Spark build, Spark fails at startup.\par
If WinUtils is missing or mismatched, Hadoop file access fails.\par
\par
2. Install JDK 17\par
Recommended: Java 17 LTS\par
Download: https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/downloads/#java17\par
Alternative: https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=17\par
Install JDK 17 and then set:\par
setx JAVA_HOME "C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-17"\par
setx PATH "%JAVA_HOME%\\bin;%PATH%"\par
Verify:\par
java -version\par
Important: do not use JDK 27 or an unsupported Java version with a typical Spark 3.x install.\par
\par
3. Install Hadoop WinUtils for Windows\par
Use a Hadoop version compatible with the Spark build.\par
For Spark 3.x, Hadoop 3.3.x is a safe choice.\par
WinUtils repository: https://github.com/cdarlint/winutils\par
Example matching version: https://github.com/cdarlint/winutils/tree/master/hadoop-3.3.4/bin\par
Apache Hadoop release page: https://downloads.apache.org/hadoop/common/\par
Create the folder:\par
C:\\hadoop\\bin\par
Copy these files into that folder:\par
winutils.exe\par
hadoop.dll\par
Set environment variables:\par
setx HADOOP_HOME "C:\\hadoop"\par
setx PATH "%HADOOP_HOME%\\bin;%PATH%"\par
Restart VS Code or the terminal after setting the variables.\par
\par
4. Use the correct environment setup in Python\par
Example:\par
import os\par
os.environ["JAVA_HOME"] = r"C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-17"\par
os.environ["HADOOP_HOME"] = r"C:\\hadoop"\par
os.environ["PATH"] = r"C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-17\\bin;C:\\hadoop\\bin;" + os.environ.get("PATH", "")\par
os.environ["SPARK_LOCAL_HOSTNAME"] = "localhost"\par
\par
5. Spark session example\par
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\par
spark = (\par
    SparkSession.builder\par
    .appName("LogHawk-FeatureEngineering")\par
    .master("local[*]")\par
    .getOrCreate()\par
)\par
\par
6. Common errors and what they mean\par
Error: ClassNotFoundException: jdk.internal.ref.Cleaner\par
Cause: incompatible Java version. Use Java 17.\par
Error: HADOOP_HOME and hadoop.home.dir are unset\par
Cause: WinUtils/Hadoop home not configured.\par
Error: UnsatisfiedLinkError: NativeIO$Windows.access0\par
Cause: missing or incompatible hadoop.dll / WinUtils install.\par
\par
7. Final checklist\par
- Java 17 installed\par
- JAVA_HOME set to C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-17\par
- Hadoop 3.3.x WinUtils downloaded\par
- C:\\hadoop\\bin contains winutils.exe and hadoop.dll\par
- HADOOP_HOME set to C:\\hadoop\par
- VS Code terminal restarted\par
- Spark session starts successfully\par
\par
8. Recommended setup pair\par
- JDK: 17\par
- Spark: 3.x\par
- Hadoop WinUtils: 3.3.x\par
\par
9. If you still get errors\par
1. Verify the Java version: java -version\par
2. Verify the Hadoop home: echo %HADOOP_HOME%\par
3. Check the files in C:\\hadoop\\bin\par
4. Make sure the WinUtils version matches the Spark/Hadoop compatibility you installed\par
5. Restart the terminal and rerun the script\par
}
